# Trunk-based development (`dev`)

- Integration trunk is **`dev`**. Do all feature work on `dev` (or a short-lived branch that merges into `dev` the same day).
- Never push feature work straight to `main`. `main` is for stable / release promotion only.
- Before coding, ensure the current branch is `dev` (or create/checkout `dev` from the latest remote `dev`/`main` as appropriate).
- Push completed work to `origin/dev` with `-u` when the branch is new.
- Keep branches short-lived; prefer direct commits on `dev` for small Closeloop tasks unless the user asks for a separate branch/PR.
- Do not force-push `dev` or `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.
